# Secrets — NEVER commit
# (This stops commits only. It does NOT stop an AI agent from reading a file.
#  Secrets live outside this folder. See docs/secrets.md.)
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.dev.vars
.dev.vars.*
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
secrets/
*-secrets/
# Broad on purpose: a note named like "design-tokens.md" is ignored too.
# Rename it, or add a !negation line for it.
*credentials*
*token*

# OS / editor cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*.swo
.vscode/
.idea/

# Obsidian local-only
.obsidian/workspace*
.obsidian/cache
.obsidian/plugins/*/data.json

# AI tool local state
.claude/cache/
.claude/sessions/
.claude/settings.local.json
.smart-env/
.wrangler/

# Personal content this template doesn't ship with
# (you'll fork and add your own — but don't push these to your fork's main branch
#  unless you're explicit about what's safe)
calendar/
inbox/screenshots/
inbox/uploads/
inbox/data/
inbox/articles/
inbox/meeting-logs/
missions/*
!missions/README.md
archive/*
!archive/README.md
atlas/handoff.md

# Hold on — read this:
# The paths above are gitignored in this PUBLIC TEMPLATE because they
# typically hold private content. When you clone this repo into your own
# private command center, you'll likely want to UN-ignore some of them
# (missions/, archive/, atlas/handoff.md) since your private repo can hold
# them safely. The public template ships with only their README files.
#
# Rule of thumb: if your repo is PRIVATE, ignore only secrets + OS cruft.
# If your repo is PUBLIC, ignore everything that contains real-world data
# about real-world businesses or people (and wiki/people/ too).
